        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Chrome 95 / FF 128 add script-closeability depending on opener]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27396</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27396"/>
        <updated>2025-08-19T07:39:17.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36379249?u=4840c2d79361800483d4c22b03d928ae33115103&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">As discussed in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18" rel="nofollow">Mozilla Bug 1316857 comment 18</a>, the concept of "same script" is vague and likely inaccurate.</p>
<p dir="auto">Additionally, to determine script-closeability, browsers switched from 'has an opener' to 'was opened by script' and that might be useful to note.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18</a></p>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<p dir="auto"><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="834043421" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/9492" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/9492/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/9492">#9492</a></p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto">My perception is these notes are usually quite short. Script-closeability also depends on the session history, so something like "Before Chrome 95, scripts could only close windows that had an opener" would be incorrect. I tried to omit this detail, but am unsure whether that made my phrasing too awkward. We could remove the notes entirely. An alternative phrasing might be "Before Chrome 95, whether a window could be closed by script depended on having an opener, not on whether it was created by web content."</p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>vinhill</name>
            <email>vinhill@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/vinhill</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2025-07-24T14:09:26.000Z</published>
    </entry>
